---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/ifric/ifric19.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope & Definitions" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Does an Extinguishment Even Occur" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Measurement — Fair Value of Equity Issued" },
        { id: "s5", label: "When Fair Value of the Equity Cannot Be Measured Reliably" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Partial Extinguishment" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Debt-for-Equity Swap" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Distinguishing Extinguishment from Modification" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "IFRIC 19 vs US GAAP" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Why debt-for-equity swaps needed a specific interpretation</div>
        <div class="principle">When a financial liability is extinguished by issuing equity instruments, the transaction has TWO sides: derecognising a liability AND issuing equity. Neither IAS 32 nor IFRS 9 explicitly addressed how to MEASURE the equity instruments issued, or how to CALCULATE the gain or loss on extinguishment. IFRIC 19 closes this gap by specifying that the gain or loss is measured as the DIFFERENCE between the carrying amount of the extinguished liability and the FAIR VALUE of the equity instruments issued.</div>
        <div class="note">Without IFRIC 19, entities could use the carrying amount of the equity instruments issued as the measurement basis — a figure that bears no relationship to the economic cost of extinguishing the debt.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Faithful representation of a barter transaction</div>
        <div class="principle">Debt-for-equity swaps are BARTER TRANSACTIONS — the entity exchanges a liability (the debt) for equity instruments. The Conceptual Framework's faithful representation principle requires that the gain or loss reflect the TRUE ECONOMIC COST of the transaction. Using the fair value of the equity issued (not the carrying amount) ensures that the gain or loss is measured at the actual economic cost — the market price of the shares given up to retire the debt.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope & Definitions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">What IFRIC 19 covers</div>
        <div class="principle">IFRIC 19 applies to the EXTINGUISHMENT of a financial liability (or a part of it) WITH EQUITY INSTRUMENTS of the entity — either the entity's own equity instruments or equity instruments of a SUBSIDIARY. The interpretation does NOT apply to: (a) transactions where the creditor is also a shareholder and the equity instruments are issued as part of a restructuring, (b) business combinations, or (c) transactions where the equity instruments are issued to employees as remuneration.</div>
        <div class="elabel">TYPICAL FACT PATTERNS</div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span>Debt-for-equity swaps in financial restructurings</span>
          <span>Convertible debt exchanges where holders elect to receive equity instead</span>
          <span>Distressed exchanges where lenders accept equity to avoid default</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Key definitions</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Extinguishment</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The derecognition of a financial liability (or part of it) when the obligation is discharged, cancelled, or expires, as defined under IFRS 9.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Equity instruments</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">Any contract that evidences a residual interest in the assets of an entity after deducting all its liabilities, as defined under IAS 32.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Does an Extinguishment Even Occur</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">The first step — derecognition analysis</div>
        <div class="principle">Before IFRIC 19's measurement rules apply, the entity must first determine whether the transaction RESULTED IN EXTINGUISHMENT of the financial liability under IFRS 9. IFRS 9's derecognition framework requires that the obligation is either: (1) discharged (the debtor no longer has a present obligation), (2) cancelled (the creditor waives the right to demand payment), or (3) expired. A debt-for-equity swap typically satisfies all three conditions — the creditor receives equity instruments instead of cash, the obligation is discharged, and the original debt instrument is cancelled.</div>
        <div class="callout warn callout--flush">⚠️ If the transaction does NOT result in derecognition — for example, if the terms are modified but the creditor retains rights — the transaction is a MODIFICATION, not an extinguishment. IFRIC 19 does NOT apply to modifications; IFRS 9's modification accounting governs those cases.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Measurement — Fair Value of Equity Issued</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">The core measurement rule</div>
        <div class="principle">IFRIC 19 specifies that the gain or loss on extinguishment is measured as: CARRIER AMOUNT OF THE EXTINGUISHED LIABILITY - FAIR VALUE OF THE EQUITY INSTRUMENTS ISSUED. The fair value of the equity instruments issued is the MARKET PRICE of those instruments at the date of extinguishment — NOT their par value, NOT their carrying amount, and NOT any other accounting-based measure.</div>
        <div class="formula-box">
          <div class="f-label">EXTINGUISHMENT GAIN/LOSS FORMULA</div>
          <div class="f-eq">Gain/(loss) = Carrying amount of extinguished liability - Fair value of equity instruments issued</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Why fair value of equity, not fair value of debt</div>
        <div class="principle">One might ask: why not measure the gain or loss as the difference between the carrying amount of the liability and the FAIR VALUE OF THE LIABILITY (which might differ if the debt was distressed)? IFRIC 19's answer is that the ECONOMIC SUBSTANCE of the transaction is that the entity is PAYING FOR THE EXTINGUISHMENT with equity — the fair value of what it gave up (equity) is the most faithful representation of the economic cost, not the potentially distressed fair value of what it got rid of (debt).</div>
        <div class="note">This approach can produce a GAIN even when the debt was traded at a discount, if the equity issued was worth MORE than the debt's carrying amount — a result that reflects the economics of the specific transaction, not a mechanical accounting rule.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>When Fair Value of the Equity Cannot Be Measured Reliably</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">The fallback measurement</div>
        <div class="principle">If the fair value of the equity instruments issued CANNOT be RELIABLY MEASURED — for example, unlisted shares with no observable market price and no reliable valuation methodology — IFRIC 19 requires the entity to measure the equity at the CARRYING AMOUNT of the extinguished liability (adjusted for any changes in credit risk since initial recognition). This fallback ensures that the gain or loss on extinguishment can always be calculated, even in the absence of reliable fair value data.</div>
        <div class="elabel">WHEN FAIR VALUE IS RELIABLE</div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span>Listed equity instruments with an active market</span>
          <span>Unlisted equity where recent transactions or reliable valuation models exist</span>
          <span>When the equity is issued to the original creditor in an arm's-length transaction</span>
        </div>
        <div class="callout info">The fallback to carrying amount of the liability means that in practice, most debt-for-equity swaps will still produce a measurable gain or loss — the only scenario where the fair value of equity is truly unmeasurable is very rare distressed situations.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Partial Extinguishment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="ctitle cn">When only part of the debt is extinguished</div>
        <div class="principle">IFRIC 19 applies equally to PARTIAL EXTINGUISHMENTS — where the equity instruments issued extinguish only a portion of the financial liability. In this case, the gain or loss is calculated ONLY for the portion extinguished: the carrying amount of the extinguished portion is compared to the fair value of the equity instruments issued for that portion. The REMAINING liability continues on the balance sheet under IFRS 9.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Allocating equity instruments to the extinguished portion</div>
        <div class="principle">Where equity instruments are issued for a PARTIAL extinguishment, the fair value of the equity instruments must be ALLOCATED between the extinguished and remaining portions of the liability. IFRIC 19 does NOT specify an allocation method, but the most common approach is to allocate pro-rata based on the relative carrying amounts of the extinguished and remaining portions.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Debt-for-Equity Swap</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="worked">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: Creditor accepts equity for 50% of debt</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company has a £10m bank loan with carrying amount £10m (no accrued interest adjustment). The company enters into a debt-for-equity swap with the bank, issuing 2m new shares to extinguish £5m of the loan. The shares are listed, and their market price on the swap date is £2.50 per share.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer"><strong>Step 1 — Fair value of equity issued:</strong> 2m shares × £2.50 = £5m<br><strong>Step 2 — Carrying amount of extinguished liability:</strong> £5m<br><strong>Step 3 — Gain/(loss) on extinguishment:</strong> £5m - £5m = £0<br><br><strong>Balance sheet impact:</strong><br>- Liability reduced by £5m (from £10m to £5m)<br>- Equity increased by £5m (share capital + share premium)<br>- No gain or loss recognised (fair value of equity = carrying amount of liability extinguished)<br><br><strong>Remaining liability:</strong> £5m, to be settled in cash per the original terms</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Distinguishing Extinguishment from Modification</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">The critical distinction</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-13-1"><span>Aspect</span><span>Extinguishment (IFRIC 19)</span><span>Modification (IFRS 9)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-13-1"><span>Definition</span><span>Original liability derecognised; new equity issued as consideration</span><span>Terms changed but obligation remains; no derecognition</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-13-1"><span>Gain/loss calculation</span><span>Carrying amount of extinguished liability - fair value of equity issued</span><span>Difference between carrying amount and present value of modified cash flows, discounted at original effective interest rate</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-13-1"><span>Equity instruments</span><span>Equity issued as consideration for extinguishment — measured at fair value</span><span>Not applicable — modification does not involve equity consideration</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-13-1"><span>Practical test</span><span>Is the original obligation discharged and replaced?</span><span>Are the terms substantially different? (10% threshold under IFRS 9)</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout warn callout--flush">⚠️ A debt-for-equity swap that is CLASSIFIED AS A MODIFICATION (not extinguishment) does NOT trigger IFRIC 19. Instead, IFRS 9's modification accounting applies — the gain or loss is calculated differently, and the equity instruments issued are accounted for under IAS 32, not IFRIC 19.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What IFRIC 19 requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>The nature and amount of the financial liability extinguished</span>
          <span>The fair value of the equity instruments issued as consideration</span>
          <span>The gain or loss recognised on extinguishment</span>
          <span>Whether the transaction was a full or partial extinguishment</span>
          <span>Any remaining terms of the liability if partially extinguished</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Judgments & Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Whether the transaction results in derecognition (extinguishment) or modification</span>
              <span>Whether the fair value of the equity instruments can be reliably measured</span>
              <span>Whether the equity instruments are issued to the original creditor or a third party</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Fair value of equity instruments when no active market exists</span>
              <span>Allocation of equity fair value between extinguished and remaining liability portions</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>IFRIC 19 vs US GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — IFRIC 19 vs ASC 470-50 (Debt with Conversion and Other Options)</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-12-1-1"><span>Feature</span><span>IFRIC 19 (IFRS)</span><span>US GAAP (ASC 470-50)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Extinguishment measurement</span><span>Fair value of equity instruments issued</span><span>Fair value of equity instruments issued</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-1-1"><span>Gain/loss calculation</span><span>Carrying amount of liability - fair value of equity issued</span><span>Same calculation — difference between carrying amount of debt and fair value of equity issued</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Partial extinguishment</span><span>Pro-rata allocation of equity fair value to extinguished portion</span><span>Similar pro-rata treatment</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-1-1"><span>Modification vs extinguishment</span><span>IFRS 9 threshold: 10% change in cash flows</span><span>Similar threshold under ASC 470-50</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Equity classification</span><span>IAS 32 governs classification of issued equity</span><span>ASC 480-10 governs whether instruments are liabilities or equity</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every IFRIC 19 event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Financial liability derecognised</span><span><span class="badge bs">SOFP</span></span><span>Removed from balance sheet at carrying amount</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Equity instruments recognised</span><span><span class="badge bs">SOFP</span></span><span>Recognised at fair value under IAS 32</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Gain or loss on extinguishment</span><span><span class="badge bp">SOPL</span></span><span>Difference between liability carrying amount and equity fair value</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Remaining liability (partial extinguishment)</span><span><span class="badge bs">SOFP</span> <span class="badge bp">SOPL</span></span><span>Continues under IFRS 9; any modification gain/loss in profit or loss</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>IFRS 9</span><span>Supplies the general derecognition and modification/extinguishment framework for financial liabilities</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>IAS 32</span><span>Governs classification and measurement of the equity instruments issued as consideration</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>IFRS 13</span><span>Supplies the fair value measurement framework applied to both the equity instruments and the extinguished liability</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Quick-reference glossary</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Extinguishment</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The derecognition of a financial liability when the obligation is discharged, cancelled, or expires — triggering IFRIC 19's measurement rules.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Debt-for-equity swap</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A transaction where a financial liability is extinguished by issuing equity instruments to the creditor — the core transaction type IFRIC 19 addresses.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <Glossary entries={[
      { term: "Extinguishment", definition: "The derecognition of a financial liability when the obligation is discharged, cancelled, or expires — triggering IFRIC 19's measurement rules." },
      { term: "Debt-for-equity swap", definition: "A transaction where a financial liability is extinguished by issuing equity instruments to the creditor — the core transaction type IFRIC 19 addresses." },
      { term: "Modification", definition: "A change to the terms of a financial liability that does NOT result in derecognition — governed by IFRS 9, not IFRIC 19." },
      { term: "Fair value of equity issued", definition: "The market price of the equity instruments issued as consideration for extinguishment, which IFRIC 19 uses to measure the gain or loss on the transaction." }
    ]} />

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.IFRIC19} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
